      "en": "Hi Evan! Today is a practice day with no new words. We bring back food and family words that need more practice and use them in short sentences about who eats and drinks what.",
      "py": "Nǐ hǎo, Evan! Jīntiān shì liànxí rì, méiyǒu xīn cí. Wǒmen bǎ xū yào duō liànxí de shíwù hé jiārén cí dài huílái, yòng duǎn jùzi shuō shéi chī shénme, hē shénme."
    },
    "blocks": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "text": "Who eats what? Food words in family sentences"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "en": "Today there are no new words. We bring back food and family words that need more practice, like apple, drink, five, and daughter, and we use them in short sentences about who eats and drinks what. Say each line out loud.",
        "py": "Jīntiān méiyǒu xīn cí. Wǒmen bǎ xū yào duō liànxí de shíwù hé jiārén cí dài huílái, bǐrú píngguǒ, hē, wǔ hé nǚ'ér, ránhòu yòng duǎn jùzi shuō shéi chī shénme, hē shénme. Měi jù dōu dàshēng shuō."
      },
      {
        "type": "vocab_card",
        "en": "apple",
        "py": "píngguǒ",
        "note_en": "Píngguǒ is 2nd tone then 3rd tone. Wǒ chī píngguǒ = I eat an apple.",
        "note_py": "Píngguǒ shì dì-èr shēng jiā dì-sān shēng. Wǒ chī píngguǒ.",
        "listen_url": "l19-pingguo.mp3"
      },
      {
        "type": "vocab_card",
        "en": "to drink",
        "py": "hē",
        "note_en": "Hē is 1st tone, high and flat. Drinks come after it: hē shuǐ, hē chá, hē niúnǎi.",
        "note_py": "Hē shì dì-yī shēng, gāo ér píng. Yǐnliào fàng zài hòumiàn: hē shuǐ, hē chá, hē niúnǎi.",
        "listen_url": "l19-he.mp3"
      },
      {
        "type": "vocab_card",
        "en": "daughter",
        "py": "nǚ'ér",
        "note_en": "Nǚ'ér: 3rd tone, then 2nd tone. The ü sound is like saying 'ee' with round lips.",
